# Waveshare ESP32-P4-WIFI6-DEV-KIT
#
# Both links on one board: 100M Ethernet (with PoE on the magjack) and an
# ESP32-C6 for WiFi 6. Build it with:
#   idf.py -B build.wifi6devkit -D SDKCONFIG=build.wifi6devkit/sdkconfig \
#          -D SDKCONFIG_DEFAULTS="sdkconfig.defaults;boards/wifi6devkit_p4.defaults" build
#
# Read off the published schematic (ESP32-P4-WIFI6-DEV-KIT-datasheet.pdf), and
# there is almost nothing to declare: every pin that matters is already the
# default, because this board wires the same parts the same way.
#   Ethernet: TX_EN 49, TXD0 34, TXD1 35, CRS_DV 28, RXD0 29, RXD1 30, MDC 31,
#             MDIO 52, REF_CLK 50 - identical to the ESP32-P4-ETH.
#   microSD: CLK 43, CMD 44, D0 39, D1 40, D2 41, D3 42, with SD1_VDD through an
#            AO3401 P-channel MOSFET on GPIO 45, so active low.
#   ESP32-C6 over SDIO: GPIO 14-19, C6_CHIP_PU from GPIO 54 through a 0R.
#   Capture I2C: SCL 8, SDA 7. BOOT button: GPIO 35. Console: CH343P on the
#   Type-C, so UART.
# 32 MB PSRAM in package and 32 MB flash, so the base partition table fits.
#
# One thing to know that is not a config: the USB OTG port is switched between
# HOST and DEVICE by a jumper. The KVM needs DEVICE - that is how it presents a
# keyboard and mouse to the target.
#
# NOT YET VERIFIED ON HARDWARE. Configured from the schematic and published so
# owners can try it.

# --- WiFi co-processor ------------------------------------------------------
# Same C6-over-SDIO arrangement as the PoE and WIFI6 boards, so the same
# esp-hosted configuration - including the guard against its eager constructor
# init, which otherwise races the microSD for the SD host.
CONFIG_KVM_WIFI=y
CONFIG_ESP_HOSTED_P4_DEV_BOARD_FUNC_BOARD=y
CONFIG_SLAVE_IDF_TARGET_ESP32C6=y
CONFIG_ESP_HOSTED_CP_TARGET_ESP32C6=y
CONFIG_ESP_HOSTED_AUTO_CALL_INIT_BEFORE_APP_MAIN=n

# --- microSD ----------------------------------------------------------------
CONFIG_KVM_SD_PWR_GPIO=45

# --- capture reset ----------------------------------------------------------
# The base default drives GPIO 23 as the TC358743's RESETN, which is how the
# ESP32-P4-ETH is wired. Here that pin is an ordinary expansion pin: the CSI
# connector carries the bridge's I2C and two camera control lines, and neither
# reaches 23. Driving it would fight whatever an owner has plugged in, and the
# C790 has its own power-on reset, so leave it alone.
CONFIG_KVM_TC358743_RST_GPIO=-1

# --- updates ----------------------------------------------------------------
CONFIG_KVM_UPDATE_URL="https://espkvm.github.io/espkvm/firmware/p4-wifi6-devkit/manifest.json"

# Which board this is: names it in the console and picks the expansion header
# the Pins tab draws.
CONFIG_KVM_BOARD_WAVESHARE_WIFI6_DEVKIT=y
